+# CLI Contract Delta: `import` and `export --format html`
+
+**Feature**: `002-import-html-export` | **Date**: 2026-11-20
+
+This document is the external interface *added* by feature 002. It amends — and does not
+replace — [feature 001's CLI contract](../../001-bookmark-manager-cli/contracts/cli-contract.md),
+which remains authoritative for everything it covers.
+
+Two statements in that document are superseded, and nothing else:
+
+> "Exactly five commands exist. There is no `update`, `import`, `tag-rename`, interactive
+> mode, colour option, pagination or configuration file."
+
+Read now as: **exactly six commands exist** — `add`, `list`, `search`, `delete`, `export`,
+`import`. There is still no `update`, `tag-rename`, interactive mode, colour option,
+pagination or configuration file.
+
+> `export --format {csv,json}`
+
+Read now as: `export --format {csv,json,html}`.
+
+Every other clause of the 001 contract — the `--db` option, the listing format, the CSV and
+JSON export bytes, the exit-status table, the single-line error rule — holds unchanged
+(FR-028).
+
+## Invocation
+
+```text
+python -m bookmarks [--db PATH] COMMAND [ARGS...]
+```
+
+`--db` remains a **global** option that must precede the command, with the same default
+(`bookmarks.db` in the current working directory) and the same creation semantics — created at
+mode `0600` if absent (FR-002, FR-003, FR-030, SR-005).
+
+---
+
+## `import FILE --format {csv,json}`
+
+Reads bookmarks from `FILE` and appends them to the collection. All-or-nothing.
+
+| Element | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| `FILE` | Positional, **required**. A path to a readable regular file of at most 33,554,432 bytes (32 MiB), holding at most 50,000 records (SR-014). Opened read-only; never executed, interpolated, or used as a shell word (SR-016, SR-017). |
+| `--format {csv,json}` | **Required.** Determines how `FILE` is parsed. Taken from this option **alone** — the file's name, extension and content are never inspected to decide the format (FR-031). Any other value, including `html` and `CSV`, is an argument error. |
+| stdout | On success, exactly `imported N\n` where `N` is the decimal count of bookmarks added — **and nothing else** (FR-038). On any failure, **empty**. |
+| stderr | Empty on success. Exactly one line otherwise (SR-018). |
+| Status | `0` on success (including `imported 0`); `2` for any argument or input-file fault; `1` if the collection is unusable. |
+
+```console
+$ python -m bookmarks --db b.db import in.json --format json
+imported 2
+$ python -m bookmarks --db b.db list
+1	https://docs.python.org	Python docs	docs,python
+2	https://example.com	Example	
+```
+
+### Accepted CSV input
+
+The format `export --format csv` writes. Strict UTF-8, no byte-order mark.
+
+```csv
+id,url,title,tags
+1,https://docs.python.org,Python docs,"docs,python"
+2,https://example.com,Example,
+```
+
+- The **first row must equal `id,url,title,tags`** exactly — same four names, same order, same
+  lower case. A reordered (`url,id,title,tags`), re-cased (`ID,URL,TITLE,TAGS`), extended or
+  truncated header is rejected, as is a file whose first row is already data.
+- Every subsequent non-empty row holds **exactly four fields**.
+- Standard CSV quoting applies, so a field holding a comma, a double quote or a newline is
+  recovered unchanged — this is what makes `export --format csv` output re-importable.
+- A single blank line at the end of the file is ignored. A blank line *between* data rows is
+  rejected.
+- The `id` field's content is discarded without being interpreted; it may be any text, or
+  empty.
+
+### Accepted JSON input
+
+The format `export --format json` writes. Strict UTF-8, no byte-order mark.
+
+```json
+[{"url": "https://docs.python.org", "title": "Python docs", "tags": ["docs", "python"]},
+ {"url": "https://example.com", "title": "Example", "tags": []}]
+```
+
+- The top-level value must be an **array**; every element must be an **object**.
+- Every element must carry **all three** of `url` (string), `title` (string) and `tags` (array
+  of strings). A missing or wrongly typed key is rejected — nothing is defaulted.
+- Any other key, `id` included, is ignored.
+
+### Record rules (identical to `add`)
+
+Each record is added exactly as `add` would add it (FR-035). A record that `add` would reject
+fails the **whole** import.
+
+| Field | Rule | Limit |
+|---|---|---|
+| `url` | Must begin with the exact lowercase `http://` or `https://` (FR-008). `ftp://`, `javascript:`, `HTTPS://`, `example.com` and `` are all rejected. | 8192 chars |
+| `title` | Stored verbatim, tabs and newlines included (FR-009). `""` is valid. | 4096 chars |
+| `tags` | CSV: the field's text. JSON: the array joined with commas. Then parsed by FR-012 — split on commas, trim each entry, drop entries that are then empty, keep each distinct tag once in first-appearance order. | 4096 chars of text, ≤ 64 tags, each ≤ 128 chars |
+
+So `",", "a,,b", " a , b ", "a,a"` and the arrays `[], ["a","a"], [" a ","b "], [""]` all
+resolve to the same tag sets `add` produces — they are **not** rejected (spec Edge Cases).
+
+### Semantics
+
+| Property | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| Order | Records are added in file order, so ascending identifier order reproduces file order (FR-036). |
+| Identifiers | Assigned by the collection's own rule (FR-007, FR-034). Any `id` in the file is ignored: a file with ids `7,8,9` imported into an empty collection produces `1,2,3`. |
+| Existing bookmarks | Never removed, modified or reordered (FR-037). |
+| Duplicates | **Never** deduplicated. A URL already in the collection, or repeated within the file, produces an additional bookmark with its own identifier (FR-037). |
+| Atomicity | All records commit together or none do. A file whose last record is invalid adds none of the earlier ones (FR-039, SR-015). |
+| Empty input | A CSV with only its header row, or the JSON document `[]`, is a **success**: `imported 0`, status 0, collection unchanged (FR-038). |
+| The input file | Never created, truncated, modified or deleted. Content, size and modification time are unchanged after both a successful and a failed import (SR-017). |
+| Side effects | No process spawned, no socket opened, no file read other than `FILE` and the collection, no reference inside `FILE` followed (SR-016). |
+
+### Failure contract
+
+| Case | Message (one line, stderr) | Status |
+|---|---|---|
+| `FILE` absent from the command line, or `--format` absent | argparse message | 2 |
+| `--format` is not `csv` or `json` | argparse message | 2 |
+| Path does not exist, is a directory, is a dangling symlink, or is not a regular file | `cannot read 'P': it is not a readable file` | 2 |
+| Path cannot be read (permissions) | `cannot read 'P': permission denied` | 2 |
+| Larger than 32 MiB | `'P' is too large to import: N bytes, at most 33554432 allowed` | 2 |
+| Not valid UTF-8 (including a byte-order mark's effects) | `cannot read 'P': it is not valid UTF-8 text` | 2 |
+| Empty file, `--format csv` | `invalid CSV: the header row is missing` | 2 |
+| Wrong CSV header | `invalid CSV: the first row must be exactly 'id,url,title,tags'` | 2 |
+| CSV row with ≠ 4 fields | `invalid CSV: row N has K fields, exactly 4 required` | 2 |
+| Blank CSV row before the end | `invalid CSV: row N is blank` | 2 |
+| Unparsable JSON (including an empty file) | `invalid JSON: the document could not be parsed` | 2 |
+| JSON nested beyond the parser's depth | `invalid JSON: the document is nested too deeply` | 2 |
+| Top-level JSON value not an array | `invalid JSON: the document must be an array of bookmark objects` | 2 |
+| JSON element not an object, or missing/mistyped `url`/`title` | `invalid JSON: record N must be an object with 'url', 'title' and 'tags'` | 2 |
+| JSON `tags` not an array of strings | `invalid JSON: record N must give 'tags' as an array of strings` | 2 |
+| More than 50,000 records | `too many bookmarks to import: at most 50000 allowed` | 2 |
+| A record `add` would reject (bad URL, oversized field) | `record N: ` + the message `add` gives for the same value | 2 |
+| Collection unusable or corrupt | the existing 001 message | **1** |
+
+In every status-2 case: **stdout is empty, no bookmark is added, and if the collection file did
+not exist it is not created.** Where both the input file and the collection are faulty, the
+input file is diagnosed first, so status 2 wins (spec Assumptions).
+
+No message contains a stack trace, an exception class name, SQL text, or any absolute path
+other than one the user supplied (SR-018). Positions are reported as **"row N"** / **"record
+N"**, 1-based, counting the CSV header as row 1 and the first JSON array element as record 1.
+
+---
+
+## `export --format {csv,json,html}`
+
+`csv` and `json` are **byte-for-byte unchanged** (FR-028, FR-040). `html` is added.
+
+| Element | Contract |
+|---|---|
+| `--format {csv,json,html}` | Required. Any other value, `HTML` included, is an argument error with status 2 (FR-040). |
+| stdout | For `html`, the page below. |
+| stderr | Empty on success. |
+| Status | `0`; `1` if the collection is unusable. |
+
+### `export --format html` output
+
+Exactly these lines, each terminated by `\n`, in this order (FR-041):
+
+```html
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html>
+<head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Bookmarks</title></head>
+<body>
+<ul>
+...one line per bookmark...
+</ul>
+</body>
+</html>
+```
+
+Between `<ul>` and `</ul>`, **exactly one line per stored bookmark in ascending identifier
+order** (FR-042):
+
+```html
+<li><a href="URL">TITLE</a> <small>TAGS</small></li>
+```
+
+| Placeholder | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `URL` | The bookmark's URL, escaped for an attribute value: `&` → `&amp;`, `<` → `&lt;`, `>` → `&gt;`, `"` → `&quot;` (FR-043). |
+| `TITLE` | The bookmark's title, escaped for element text: `&`, `<`, `>`. Empty when the bookmark has no title. |
+| `TAGS` | The bookmark's tags joined with commas in ascending code-point order — **identical** to the `tags` field of `export --format csv` and the fourth field of a listing line — then escaped for element text. Empty when the bookmark has no tags. |
+
+Note the single space between `</a>` and `<small>`, and that the `<li>` line is written even
+when both the title and the tag list are empty: `<li><a href="URL"></a> <small></small></li>`.
+
+Text containing none of the escapable characters appears **literally**, so:
+
+```html
+<li><a href="https://docs.python.org">Python docs</a> <small>docs,python</small></li>
+```
+
+holds byte-for-byte.
+
+An **empty collection** prints the skeleton with no `<li>` line between `<ul>` and `</ul>`, and
+exits 0 (FR-044).
+
+### Guarantees
+
+- The page is well-formed whatever the stored text contains, and a standard HTML parser
+  recovers each stored URL, title and tag string unchanged (FR-043, SC-014).
+- Stored data can never become markup: a title of `<script>alert(1)</script>` appears as
+  escaped text, and a `"` in a title or URL cannot break out of the `href` attribute (SR-012).
+- Output is **streamed** — peak memory does not grow with the collection size (SR-019).
+- A title containing a literal newline (which FR-009 stores verbatim) puts that newline inside
+  the link text. The page stays well-formed; the one-`<li>`-per-line shape is broken by that
+  bookmark alone, as the spec's Edge Cases accept.
+- The page carries no CSS, no JavaScript, no identifier column, no heading, no counts and no
+  external resource, and it is **not** the Netscape bookmark-file format browsers import
+  (spec Assumptions).
+
+---
+
+## Exit statuses (whole tool, after this feature)
+
+| Status | Meaning | Changed by this feature? |
+|---|---|---|
+| `0` | Success, including `imported 0` and an empty HTML page | `import` and `html` added |
+| `1` | The collection could not be used: bad `--db` path, missing parent directory, corrupt or unreadable database | no |
+| `2` | Invalid input: unknown command or option, missing argument, unsupported `--format`, malformed `delete ID`, oversized input, invalid URL — **and every `import` input-file fault** | `import` faults added |
+| `3` | `delete ID` where no bookmark has that identifier | no |
+
+`import` never returns 3.
