+# Requirements → Test Matrix
+
+**Feature**: `002-import-html-export` | **Date**: 2026-11-20
+
+Constitution Principle III requires every functional requirement to map to at least one
+automated `pytest` test; Principle V requires every security requirement to map to at least
+one test **including a negative case**. SC-010 requires 100% coverage of FR-028…FR-044 and
+SR-012…SR-019 plus every acceptance scenario in User Stories 1–3.
+
+This matrix is the artifact the Test gate and the Review gate are audited against. The named
+test functions are the planned contract; `/speckit-tasks` turns each row into work.
+
+**Coverage**: 17 FR + 8 SR = **25 requirements, 25 mapped, 0 unmapped, 0 planned skips.**
+Feature 001's 38 requirements keep their existing 001 tests, which are **not edited** by this
+feature (SC-011) — see the Compatibility section below for how that is proved mechanically.
+
+## Functional requirements
+
+| Req | Test file | Test function | Assertion |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| FR-028 | integration/test_compatibility.py | `test_existing_commands_are_byte_identical` | For a fixed seeded collection, `add`/`list`/`search`/`delete`/`export --format csv`/`export --format json` produce the stdout, stderr and status recorded as golden values in the test; the whole 001 suite is also run unmodified |
+| FR-029 | integration/test_compatibility.py | `test_pre_feature_database_still_works` / `test_post_feature_database_works_with_old_commands` | A database built with only 001's statements is read by all six commands with no migration; a database written by `import` is listed, searched, deleted from and exported correctly |
+| FR-030 | contract/test_cli_surface_v2.py | `test_sixth_subcommand_exists` / `test_import_uses_global_db_option` / `test_import_creates_missing_database` | `import f --format csv` parses with `command == "import"`; `--db` before the command is honoured; a missing database file is created at mode `0600` by a successful import |
+| FR-031 | contract/test_cli_surface_v2.py | `test_import_requires_file_and_format` / `test_import_rejects_other_formats` / `test_format_is_not_inferred_from_extension` | Omitting `FILE` or `--format` exits 2; `html`, `CSV`, `xml`, `""` exit 2; a JSON document named `x.csv` imported with `--format json` succeeds, and the same file with `--format csv` exits 2 |
+| FR-032 | unit/test_import_records.py | `test_csv_header_and_four_fields_required` / `test_csv_quoting_round_trips` / `test_csv_tags_field_uses_add_rules` | Header must equal `id,url,title,tags`; rows of 3 and 5 fields exit 2; a field holding a comma, a `"` and a `\n` is recovered unchanged; `"a,,b"` → tags `a,b` |
+| FR-033 | unit/test_import_records.py | `test_json_array_of_objects_required` / `test_json_requires_all_three_keys_with_types` / `test_json_extra_keys_ignored` | Top-level object/string/number/`null` exit 2; non-object element exits 2; each of missing/mistyped `url`,`title`,`tags` exits 2; `{"id":7,"colour":"red",...}` imports with the extras discarded |
+| FR-034 | integration/test_story5_import.py | `test_file_ids_are_ignored` | US1 AS4 — a file with ids `7,8,9` into an empty collection yields ids `1,2,3`; a file with absent and non-numeric `id` fields imports identically |
+| FR-035 | unit/test_import_records.py | `test_imported_record_matches_add_exactly` / `test_degenerate_tag_values` / `test_invalid_url_fails_whole_import` | For a parametrised set of (url, title, tags) the rows and tag links written by `import` equal those written by `add` with the same values; `","`, `"a,,b"`, `" a , b "`, `"a,a"`, `[]`, `["a","a"]`, `[" a ","b "]`, `[""]` give the documented tag sets; `ftp://`, `javascript:`, `HTTPS://`, `example.com`, `""` each exit 2 with nothing stored |
+| FR-036 | integration/test_story5_import.py | `test_ids_follow_file_order` | US1 AS1/AS3 — ascending id order reproduces file order for both formats; importing into a collection holding 1 and 2 assigns 3,4,5 in file order |
+| FR-037 | integration/test_story5_import.py | `test_existing_bookmarks_untouched` / `test_import_never_deduplicates` | US1 AS3 — prior rows, titles and tag links byte-identical after import; a URL already stored and a URL repeated twice in the file each produce an extra bookmark |
+| FR-038 | contract/test_import_contract.py | `test_success_prints_only_the_count` / `test_empty_input_is_success` | stdout is exactly `imported 2\n`, stderr empty, status 0; US1 AS7 — a CSV header alone and the document `[]` print `imported 0\n`, status 0, collection unchanged |
+| FR-039 | contract/test_import_contract.py | `test_every_input_fault_exits_two_with_nothing_stored` | Parametrised over every row of the failure table in [cli-contract.md](./cli-contract.md#failure-contract): status 2, stdout empty, exactly one stderr line, zero new rows, zero new tag links. US1 AS5/AS6 |
+| FR-040 | contract/test_cli_surface_v2.py | `test_export_accepts_three_formats` / `test_export_rejects_other_formats` | `csv`/`json`/`html` all parse and exit 0; `HTML`, `xml`, `""` exit 2. US2 AS6 is covered by FR-028's golden-value test |
+| FR-041 | contract/test_html_format.py | `test_page_skeleton_is_exact` | The output's first five lines and last three lines equal the FR-041 skeleton byte-for-byte, each `\n`-terminated; no other line lies outside `<ul>`/`</ul>`. US2 AS1 |
+| FR-042 | contract/test_html_format.py | `test_one_li_line_per_bookmark_in_id_order` / `test_li_line_is_byte_exact` / `test_empty_title_and_tags_still_emit_a_line` / `test_html_tags_match_csv_tags` | Count of `<li>` lines equals the bookmark count and their order is ascending id; US2 AS2's line holds byte-for-byte; US2 AS3's `<li><a href="URL"></a> <small></small></li>`; for a seeded collection each line's `<small>` text equals that bookmark's `tags` field from `export --format csv` |
+| FR-043 | unit/test_html_escaping.py | `test_element_text_escapes_amp_lt_gt` / `test_attribute_also_escapes_quote` / `test_ampersand_is_escaped_first` / `test_unescapable_text_is_literal` | `&<>` → `&amp;&lt;&gt;` in text; `"` → `&quot;` in the `href`; a stored `&amp;` becomes `&amp;amp;` (proving `&` is replaced before `<`); text with none of those characters is unchanged. Round-trip through `html.parser` in security/test_security_html_escaping.py. US2 AS4 |
+| FR-044 | contract/test_html_format.py | `test_empty_collection_prints_bare_skeleton` | US2 AS5 — output is exactly the eight skeleton lines, no `<li>`, status 0, stderr empty |
+
+## Security requirements
+
+Each row names the **negative** case, as Principle V requires.
+
+| Req | Baseline control | Test file | Test function | Negative assertion |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| SR-012 | No string-built interpretation (encode for context) | security/test_security_html_escaping.py | `test_stored_data_cannot_become_markup` / `test_html_parser_recovers_originals` | A collection holding title `<script>alert(1)</script>`, title `" onmouseover=x`, title `a & b`, and a URL containing `"` and `&` produces a page with **no** raw `<script>` and no unescaped `"` inside any `href`; `html.parser.HTMLParser` recovers every original URL, title and tag string exactly (also SC-014) |
+| SR-013 | Untrusted input, allow-list | security/test_security_import_shape.py | `test_malformed_shapes_are_rejected_with_nothing_stored` | Parametrised over: wrong CSV header, reordered header, upper-case header, a 3-field row, a 5-field row, a blank row between rows, a top-level JSON object, a non-object array element, a missing `title`, `tags` as a string, `tags` holding a number, invalid UTF-8 bytes, a UTF-8 BOM, a zero-byte file. Each: status 2, one stderr line, collection unchanged, **and the database file's bytes and mtime unchanged** (or still absent if it did not exist) |
+| SR-014 | Resource limits | security/test_security_import_limits.py | `test_file_one_byte_over_limit_rejected` / `test_record_count_over_limit_rejected` / `test_each_field_limit_rejected_one_char_over` / `test_deeply_nested_json_rejected` | A 32 MiB + 1 file; a 50,001-record file; a record with a 8193-char URL, a 4097-char title, a 4097-char tag text, 65 tags, a 129-char tag — each exits 2 with nothing stored; `"[" * 100000 + "]" * 100000` exits 2 with one stderr line and **no** `RecursionError` traceback escaping |
+| SR-015 | — (atomicity, extends SR-009) | security/test_security_import_atomicity.py | `test_last_record_invalid_adds_none_of_the_first_99` / `test_storage_failure_mid_write_rolls_back` / `test_next_add_identifier_is_unaffected` | 100 valid records with an invalid URL in record 100 → zero new rows, zero new tag links; a storage failure injected part-way through the transaction leaves the collection byte-identical with no orphan tag row; after a failed import of 5 records, the next `add` receives the identifier it would have received without the import |
+| SR-016 | No string-built interpretation / path handling | security/test_security_import_no_execution.py | `test_file_content_is_never_executed_or_fetched` | A file whose fields hold `$(touch /tmp/x)`, `` `id` ``, `; rm -rf /`, `../../etc/passwd`, `{{7*7}}` and `http://127.0.0.1:1/unreachable` imports successfully with every value stored as **literal text**; `socket.socket`, `socket.create_connection` and `os.posix_spawn` are monkeypatched to fail the test if called; no new file appears anywhere under `tmp_path` |
+| SR-017 | File permissions / no residual files | security/test_security_import_readonly.py | `test_input_file_is_untouched` / `test_no_extra_files_created` | After a **successful** and after a **failed** import, `FILE`'s bytes, `st_size` and `st_mtime_ns` are unchanged; the database's directory holds only the database file (no journal, no temp file, no copy); a `FILE` opened from a read-only directory still imports |
+| SR-018 | Output hygiene | security/test_security_import_messages.py | `test_every_failure_is_one_clean_line` | Parametrised over every documented status-2 import failure **and** the unusable-database and corrupt-database cases: exactly one stderr line, ≥ 3 words, and none of `SELECT`, `INSERT`, `DELETE`, `UPDATE`, `PRAGMA`, `FROM bookmarks`, `VALUES (` nor, case-insensitively, `traceback`, `sqlite`, `file "`, `line `, `.py`; the only absolute path permitted in the line is one the test passed in |
+| SR-019 | Resource limits | security/test_security_html_streaming.py | `test_html_export_of_50k_is_memory_bounded` / `test_import_memory_does_not_grow_with_collection` | `tracemalloc` peak for `export --format html` of 50,000 bookmarks is within the same ceiling as 5,000 (reusing 001's discarding-sink harness); importing a 50,000-record file into a collection already holding 50,000 bookmarks has a peak within the same ceiling as importing it into an empty collection. Both marked `slow` |
+
