+| SC-012 | contract/test_import_contract.py | `test_every_input_fault_exits_two_with_nothing_stored` — the same parametrised table, asserting zero partial imports, zero silent skips, zero status-0 results on bad input |
+| SC-013 | integration/test_performance_v2.py | `test_html_export_of_10k_under_one_second` / `test_import_of_10k_under_ten_seconds` — both marked `slow` |
+| SC-014 | security/test_security_html_escaping.py | `test_html_parser_recovers_originals` — `html.parser` on the first attempt, over a collection seeded with `<`, `>`, `&`, `"` and non-ASCII characters in titles, URLs and tags |
+| SC-015 | security/test_security_stdlib_only.py (**feature 001, unedited**) | `test_whole_package_imports_only_these_standard_modules` / `test_shipped_files_are_the_five_planned_modules` — both still pass because this feature adds no module and no import outside the existing whitelist (see research.md R1, R2) |
+
+## Compatibility: how SC-011 is proved mechanically
+
+1. **No feature-001 test file is edited.** `test_feature_001_test_files_are_unmodified`
+   records their digests, so an edit is a test failure rather than a silent regression.
+2. The two 001 tests that *could* have been broken by this feature are the ones that pin the
+   package's shape — `test_shipped_files_are_the_five_planned_modules` and
+   `test_whole_package_imports_only_these_standard_modules`. The design keeps the shipped file
+   list at five and the import set within the existing whitelist precisely so that both keep
+   passing (research.md R1, R2).
+3. `test_no_sixth_subcommand` (001) asserts only that `frobnicate` is rejected, not that the
+   parser has five subparsers, so adding `import` leaves it green.
+4. New fixtures needed by this feature (a `write_file(name, text_or_bytes)` helper and a
+   `database_fingerprint(path)` helper) are **added** to `tests/conftest.py`. No existing
+   fixture is renamed or changed, so every 001 test resolves the same fixtures as before.
